KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp98
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ explicitly instantiated: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.explicit]/1, /10: `template int box<char>::put(long);' is an
explicit instantiation definition of a member function template
specialization.  With it, the specialization has no body ("no body for
callee box<char>::put"); without it, the implicit instantiation works.
libstdc++ explicitly instantiates basic_ostream's _M_insert this way
(bits/ostream.tcc, with matching `extern template' declarations).  Also
fails on bin53.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails
only its WRONG assertion.
